                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "\"Rotate and navigate a colorful world\" seems quite a short description for a game, so we'll stick with that. The whole Steam store page does not mention anything more, not even the controls or what the game is about, apart from a brief reference to a \"platformer\".\nIf one is interested in this game's 10 achievements he will get them within 2 hours in my opinion, but depending on your skills you'll probably be able to get them even within 1 hour - you have just to complete all the levels which, as you may have understood so far, are.. yeah, well, just 10.\nThe soundtrack is some random ambient track, while the options are just linked to a small scale that lets us lower or raise the mouse sensitivity.\nThe WASD keys will be used to move and shift, to run. Non remappable and I don't even know if it supports gamepads or not - keyboard reviews here most of the times =P\nWhy the mouse sensitivity then? Well, the game is a 3D platformer in which we will see only in front of us, thus it will be extremely important to focus on where to jump and when.\nLet's not talk that much about the fact that we aren't told that the space key is used to jump..\nWell, the game isn't that hard - once you get used to the mouse sensitivity and the shift key to run and make longer jumps you'll get through the whole game within, as I said, 2 hours or less.\nAnd it costs 2€.\nPlus, it's a standard 3D platformer without literally anything to add if compared to tons of similar games. The usual first person perspective, jumps on a colorful block world and little else.\nAnd for weird reasons, pink blocks will transform once you hit the spacebar.. don't ask me why.\nAll in all it's a somehow acceptable approach to an indie 3D platformer, but it really adds nothing to the user's experience and it consists of a few levels all looking the same.\nAnd this is my 600th review I think.",
